          "kinds": null,
          "prompt_rule": "Five items, each a scene as picture: {kind:\"scene\", describe} of one object placed by another (a cat under a table), placed in, on, under, near or behind it, never above, over, beside or next to. The describe names the floor and the thing's own legs or base (\"a ball on the floor under a chair\", \"a bird on top of the roof\"). Never a bird or animal in or on a tree, or in any scene where both in and on read true (a bird among the leaves of a branch is both): use in only for a thing inside a container (box, basket, bag, cup). Stem: \"The cat is ____ the table.\" Answer: that one word. v35 (bd-5jmnfj.4.58.9): in each scene only one of the five words is true; near is true of anything at, under, behind or beside another thing, so put the thing clearly apart for near; for an in, on, under or behind answer draw the position plainly, and scheme.accept never lists near (the child reads the picture for that position). Repeat one word across two items, so the last item cannot be found by using each word once. The picture is a plain black-outline drawing a child names at once: never a thing whose outline alone is unreadable (egg, ball, plate, cup, watch, bench, box). A small object placed in a scene is drawn large and in front.",
